    {
      "file": "Zend/zend_compile.c",
      "function": "zend_compile_attributes",
      "line": 5731,
      "code": "zend_ast_list *args = el->child[1] ? zend_ast_get_list(el->child[1]) : NULL;",
      "note": "First project-code materialization of the attacker-controlled attribute arguments on the vulnerable path. For the staged parameter attribute, this statement produces a `ZEND_AST_ARG_LIST` with two children: a valid first argument (`self::class`) and the invalid dynamic class-constant second argument (`s->getAtelf::FOO`).",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "Zend/zend_attributes.c",
      "function": "zend_add_attribute",
      "line": null,
      "code": "",
      "note": "The flexible `attr->argv[]` storage is allocated from raw `pemalloc()` memory and vulnerable code does not initialize each slot to `IS_UNDEF` before later population and cleanup. Because the attribute is inserted into the attribute hash before all arguments are compiled, any fatal error during argument compilation leaves trailing `argv[]` slots uninitialized but still subject to destruction. The fix adds a loop that applies `ZVAL_UNDEF(&attr->argv[i])` for every declared argument.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "Zend/zend_attributes.c",
      "function": "zend_add_attribute",
      "line": 104,
      "code": "",
      "note": "The flexible `attr->argv[]` storage is allocated from raw `pemalloc()` memory and vulnerable code does not initialize each slot to `IS_UNDEF` before later population and cleanup. Because the attribute is inserted into the attribute hash before all arguments are compiled, any fatal error during argument compilation leaves trailing `argv[]` slots uninitialized but still subject to destruction. The fix adds a loop that applies `ZVAL_UNDEF(&attr->argv[i])` for every declared argument.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "Zend/zend_types.h",
      "function": "zend_gc_delref",
      "line": null,
      "code": "",
      "note": "ASan crash site. `zend_gc_delref()` dereferences the bogus `zend_refcounted_h *` extracted from the uninitialized `attr->argv[1]` slot during attribute cleanup, producing the reported wild-address READ.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
